This section covers the Typedown language itself, independent of any theme or tooling. Each page builds on the previous one.

- [Vault and documents](01-vault-and-documents): project structure, file anatomy, and how content forms a graph
- [Schemas and types](02-schemas-and-types): defining node types, the type system, expressions, and file references
- [Frontmatter](03-frontmatter): all built-in `_` directives and how frontmatter fields are resolved
- [Markdown body](04-markdown-body): full syntax reference for the document body
- [Type system](05-type-system): primitive types, compound types, optionals, and type expressions
- [Icons](06-icons): the `icon` module and all available icon names
- [Vault query API](07-vault-query): query pages, schemas, and directory listings at runtime
